    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build passes and both acceptance tests are green.\n\n## Summary\n\nChanged owner deletion from a hard-delete to a soft-delete. `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` now flags the record instead of removing it, and the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks ignore flagged owners.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`), defaulting to `Boolean.FALSE`, with getter/setter. A newly created owner is therefore `deleted: false`.\n\n2. **`DeleteOwner.java`** \u2014 instead of `repository.delete(owner)`, it now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s, retaining the row. The DELETE pipeline still ends in `RespondWithNoContent` (204, a 2xx), and `LoadOwner`/`GET` continue to return the row with `deleted: true`.\n\n3. **`EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java`** \u2014 skips owners flagged deleted, so a normally-blocking household/contact duplicate is allowed when the only match has been soft-deleted (the core spec requirement).\n\n4. **`FlagPossibleDuplicate.java`** \u2014 likewise skips deleted owners for the soft-duplicate flag.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `deleted` (boolean, readOnly) property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically into GET/create responses.\n\n6. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `deleted` column defaulting to false, so seed rows read back as not-deleted and the JPA entity persists the flag (the test profile uses hsqldb with `ddl-auto=none`, driven by `schema.sql`).\n\nTest results: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` both pass, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
